<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Göppingen</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Göppingen is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the River Fils east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stuttgart">Stuttgart</a>. Lying below the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> hill, the ancestral seat of the Staufer emperors, it became an industrial town in the nineteenth century, and the toy and model railway maker <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marklin">Märklin</a>, founded there in 1859, still has its headquarters in the town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/goppingen.jpg" alt="Göppingen" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Stadt Faurndau · CC BY-SA 2.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Faurndau_Stiftskirche.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
